{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Status: claimed, change committed, Gerrit upload BLOCKED on host credentials\n\n### Plan-review gate\n\nThe first review blocked on P4 `oversize` only (description 8218 chars vs the 8000 cap). The\ndescription was tightened to 6118 chars with the narration moved into the preceding comment; no\nwork was split. The advisory P6 finding (a `grep` verify command that inspected output without\nasserting) was also addressed by switching the affected criteria to `grep -q` / an explicit\ncount.\n\nRe-review `1789496660182743540` returned **PASS**, attestation **certified**, signed at\n`1789496653499432084` against `verified_at_sha 5c2d3e664fad5dab42109df9e11d7154282fa217`\n(currency basis `file_impact`). The ticket was then claimed normally — no `--force` was used at\nany point.\n\n### The change\n\nCommitted in a worktree branched from `origin/main` (5c2d3e664fa):\n\n- branch: `serena-mcp-project-scope`\n- commit: `5583b266a4`\n- `Change-Id: Ibcecdc89b11ce341e975aaa39945e7014a5b3005`\n- `Signed-off-by: Joe Oakhart <joeoakhart@navapbc.com>`, trailer `rebar-ticket: f920-dc37-28e4-4a91`\n- 3 files changed, 78 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)\n\nThe pre-commit gate passed (ruff check + format-check, mypy, 50/72 commit-message wrap).\n\n### Acceptance-criteria evidence\n\n- **AC1 / AC2 — entry shape and no git-build launcher.**\n  `pytest tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_client_configs.py -k serena -q` →\n  `1 passed, 10 deselected`. The regression assertion was separately demonstrated to fail when\n  the entry is reverted to `command: \"uvx\"` with a `git+` arg.\n- **AC3 — workspace-scoped, not user-scoped.** `copilot mcp list` from the repo root:\n\n  ```\n  User servers:\n    atlassian (local)\n\n  Workspace servers:\n    rebar (http)\n    serena (local)\n  ```\n\n  The same command from `$HOME` lists only `User servers: atlassian (local)` — no serena.\n- **AC4 — live headless run initializes serena.** Fresh run logged to\n  `~/.copilot/logs/process-1789497249299-8177.log`:\n  `grep -c \"MCP server connection failed\"` → **0**, and the log carries\n  `server_info: Some(Implementation { name: \"Serena\", title: None, version: \"1.7.1.dev0\" … })`.\n  Note for anyone re-running this check: the log escapes its quotes, so the matching pattern is\n  `grep -q 'name: \\\\\"Serena\\\\\"' <log>` (or `grep -q 'name: .*Serena'`), not the single-wildcard\n  form written in AC4.\n- **AC5 — docs.**\n  `grep -q \"uv tool install --from git+https://github.com/oraios/serena serena-agent\" docs/mcp-client-setup.md`\n  exits 0.\n- **AC6 — Gerrit upload: NOT met. Blocked, see below.**\n\n### Blocker: no Gerrit credential exists on this host\n\nThe change is committed and ready to upload, and the `gerrit` remote is now configured as\n`https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/a/rebar`, but the push cannot authenticate. Probed\nexhaustively:\n\n- `git credential fill` for `rebar.solutions.navateam.com` → `fatal: unable to get password from\n  user`; the only keychain entries are for `github.com` and an ECR host, and\n  `credential.interactive` is set to `never`.\n- No `~/.netrc`.\n- SSH on 29418 now completes the host-key exchange but returns\n  `Permission denied (publickey)`; `ssh-add -l` reports `The agent has no identities` and\n  `~/.ssh` contains no key files.\n- No other clone or worktree on the host has ever had a `gerrit` remote.\n\nUploading needs a human to supply a Gerrit HTTP password (Gerrit → Settings → HTTP Credentials)\nor register an SSH key. Once available, the remaining step is a single command from the\nworktree: `git push gerrit HEAD:refs/for/main`, followed by recording the change number here.\nPer the ticket's own AC6, `LLM-Review +1` / `Verified +1` and Submit are out of scope this\nsession because the pipeline is known-blocked.\n\n### Note on `rebar verify-commit-ticket --rev HEAD`\n\nIt reports this ticket id as unresolved locally. That is a stale local mirror, not a bad\ntrailer: the checkout's `refs/heads/tickets` is behind (`7dd7596884f`) while `origin/tickets`\nnow contains this ticket through `a462459f06b ticket: CLAIM f920-dc37-28e4-4a91`. The local\nbranch was left untouched rather than fast-forwarded with raw git, per the tracker's\nno-ad-hoc-raw-git rule."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789497294310999006,"uuid":"ca6d3a3a-f0a0-4f71-82fa-638ab6a2b4bd"}